2026-11-19 21:28:26 - Agent_20261119212600 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 10 CodeQL results for py/setuptools-unsafe-extract (CWE-022).

Findings:
- setuptools/archive_util.py:103/195 and setuptools/wheel.py:119 — marked manual review (mr). These are the genuine archive *extraction* sinks. Both zip (unpack_zipfile → _unpack_zipfile_obj) and tar (_iter_open_tar → tarobj._extract_member) paths do contain mitigations: names starting with '/' or containing '..' path segments are skipped, and tar sym/hard links are resolved via _resolve_tar_file_or_dir. wheel.py:119 reuses _unpack_zipfile_obj. Residual risk remains for Windows backslash-based traversal ('..\..\x') since the filters only split on '/', and _extract_member is a private tarfile API whose exact containment semantics vary across Python versions — hence mr rather than tp.
- pkg_resources/__init__.py:1761 (ZipManifests.build) — fp, only reads namelist()/getinfo() into a dict, no filesystem writes.
- setuptools/_distutils/archive_util.py:116, :176, :180 and setuptools/command/bdist_egg.py:454, setuptools/command/easy_install.py:1577 — fp, archive *creation* sinks (tarfile.open(...,'w'), zipfile.ZipFile(...,'w'), z.write/zip.write); no attacker-controlled extraction.
- setuptools/command/upload_docs.py:79 — fp, creates a zip from a local docs directory for upload.

No new independent vulnerabilities were identified beyond the flagged group.
